.git
.github
.claude
.cursor
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Nested env files too: apps/web/.env.local would otherwise ride along with
# `COPY apps/web`, and any NEXT_PUBLIC_* value in it would be baked into the
# client bundle.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
.venv
venv
node_modules
.next
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.pnpm-store
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
# Bare patterns only match at the build-context root, so nested caches (for
# example migrations/__pycache__) need the recursive form or host .pyc files
# end up baked into the image.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
# The same applies to the web workspace: apps/web/.next and
# apps/web/node_modules would otherwise ride along with `COPY apps/web`.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.pnpm-store
**/.mypy_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
logs
tmp
temp
coverage
htmlcov
*.log
.DS_Store
